<title>PERU: Peru's Feb cotton output slips to 8,685 tonnes.</title>
<headline>Peru's Feb cotton output slips to 8,685 tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's February cotton production fell to 8,685 tonnes from 9,404 tonnes in the same month last year, the Agriculture Ministry said Monday.</p>
<p>Production for the first two months of the year fell to 9,686 tonnes compared with 12,125 tonnes in the same period last year, the ministry said in its monthly report.</p>
<p>Imports of cotton rose in February 38.6 percent to $3.16 million, while imports for the first two months rose 18.9 percent $6.26 million, the ministry said.</p>
<p>According to the ministry's latest figures, exports of cotton in January fell 22.6 percent to $18.08 million.</p>
<p>((-- Saul Hudson, Lima newsroom 511 221-2134))</p>
</text>
